<p>
  Vartech's lux meter range covers two models - the V 6610 B and V 6610+ - that split along a single practical line: fixed sensor with finer resolution and wider range, or a detachable flexible sensor for measuring in places the meter body itself can't reach. Both cover general lighting measurement work; which one to buy depends on where and how you'll actually be taking readings.
</p>

<h2 id="fixed-vs-detachable">Fixed Sensor or Detachable Flexible Sensor?</h2>

<p>
  The V 6610 B has its sensor built into the meter body - simpler to use for straightforward readings where the meter itself can be positioned at the measurement point. The V 6610+ instead has a detachable sensor head on an approximately 15 cm coiled lead, supplied in a protective holster - letting you position the sensor independently of the meter body. This matters in confined or awkward locations: measuring illuminance inside an enclosure, close to a fitting where the full meter body won't fit, or at a work surface while holding the display at a readable angle.
</p>

<Callout type="tip" title="Think about where the sensor needs to physically sit">
  If your measurement points are all open, accessible surfaces (a desk, a room's general illuminance), the fixed-sensor V 6610 B is simpler and needs no cable management. If you're regularly measuring in tight spots, inside equipment, or at awkward angles, the V 6610+'s detachable sensor removes the physical constraint of the meter body itself.
</Callout>

<h2 id="range-resolution">Range and Resolution</h2>

<p>
  The V 6610 B covers a wider 0-199999 Lux range with finer resolution stepping (0.1 Lux below 200 Lux, 1 Lux above), and ±4% accuracy when calibrated against a standard tungsten flat lamp at 2856 K. The V 6610+ covers 0.1 to 200,000 Lux as a 3½-digit (2000-count) auto-ranging instrument, with accuracy varying by range and resolution setting (±(3%+10d) to ±(5%+10d) depending on the reading). For general lighting-level surveys and compliance checks against a lux specification, both cover the practical working range comfortably - the V 6610 B's finer resolution and tighter accuracy matter more when you need to document a precise reading rather than confirm a level is broadly within spec.
</p>

<h2 id="unit-selection">Lux/FC Selection and Data Features</h2>

<p>
  Both models offer Lux/FC (foot-candle) unit switching, Data Hold, and Min/Max hold. The V 6610 B adds a data recording facility; the V 6610+ adds Auto data recording and a REL (relative/zero-reference) function, useful for measuring a light-level difference against a reference point rather than an absolute value. Both run on readily available batteries (9 V for the V 6610 B, 2× AAA for the V 6610+) with backlit displays for low-light readability.
</p>

<h2 id="quick-reference">Quick Reference by Use Case</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>General lighting surveys, open/accessible measurement points</strong>: V 6610 B - wider range, finer resolution.</li>
  <li><strong>Confined spaces, awkward angles, inside fittings or enclosures</strong>: V 6610+ - detachable flexible sensor.</li>
  <li><strong>Precise documented readings against a lux specification</strong>: V 6610 B's tighter accuracy and finer resolution.</li>
  <li><strong>General compliance checks where broad range coverage matters most</strong>: either model comfortably covers standard lighting-design lux levels.</li>
</ul>

